From 10670ec4d67e4468c65cda679dfd37a2c082be71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Mutai <official.daniel.mutai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 09:57:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(barcode-scanner): fix stale scanning state and post-scan
 404

The barcode scanner had two bugs:

1. The native BarcodeDetector detection loop read `scanning` from a
   stale closure captured when the effect first ran (before
   setScanning(true) had taken effect), so the loop exited on its
   first check and never rescheduled itself via requestAnimationFrame.
   The camera would stream but nothing was ever scanned. Fixed by
   tracking scanning state in a ref (scanningRef) that the detection
   loop reads synchronously, plus a handledRef guard against
   double-fires across consecutive frames.

2. On a successful or failed barcode lookup, the sheet navigated to
   /inventory/{id} and /inventory/new?barcode=... - neither route
   exists in this app (inventory add/edit is sheet-based on /inventory
   itself), so both outcomes 404'd. Fixed by routing to /inventory with
   query params (?scannedItemId=... / ?action=add&barcode=...) that
   page.tsx already has a pattern for handling.

Supporting changes:
- inventory/page.tsx: handle scannedItemId by looking the item up in
  the already-loaded inventory list (so EditItemSheet gets a fully
  populated item, not a partial API response), with a dismissible
  notice if the item cannot be found. Pass scanned barcode through to
  AddItemSheet.
- AddItemSheet.tsx: accept initialBarcode prop, prefill + show an
  editable barcode field on the first variant, include it in the
  create payload.
- inventory.service.ts / create-product.dto.ts: declare the barcode
  field on the variant type/DTO for correctness. The backend service
  was already reading and persisting v.barcode - it just was not
  declared on the DTO (no whitelist/forbidNonWhitelisted validation is
  configured, so this is a type-safety fix, not a behavior change).

No backend routes, env vars, or deploy config touched. Verified with
tsc --noEmit (0 errors) on the frontend workspace.
